   "sub": "Use a correlation matrix to spot columns that say the same thing, see why the determinant and rank warn about them, compare rows by distance and catch rows that are strange only in combination.",
   "simple": "Cleaning is not only fixing typos. Some problems only show up when you look at the table as a **matrix**: two columns that carry the same information, a column on such a big scale that it dominates every distance, a row whose individual values look fine but whose combination is impossible. The tools are a few lines of linear algebra.",
