       "say": "**Tests for data**. Write down what must be true of the clean table and check it in code: no duplicates, ages in range, cities from a known list, spend positive, dates that are real dates. They are cheap to run and they **fail loudly** (`assert` stops the pipeline) instead of letting a bad value flow into a chart and a decision. Next month a new city spelling \"Bombay\" would make the third check fail on the day, rather than months later when someone asks why Mumbai's sales dropped.",
