       "say": "**Model-ready features.** Missing ages and visits get a **flag column each** (`age_missing`, `visits_missing`) and are then filled with the median; spend is filled likewise; segment becomes three 0/1 columns. The result is **4,000 rows by 8 columns**: **age, spend, visits, age_missing, visits_missing, segment_new, segment_regular, segment_vip**, with no missing values left and every column numeric. The repeat rate is **0.536**, so the classes are balanced enough for AUC to be a fair score. In a production pipeline the medians would be learned on the training rows only and saved with the model (the last lesson); here the split happens at the scoring step to keep the case short, and that shortcut is itself worth fixing before real use.",
