       "say": "**The expensive mistake: leaving the repeats in.** Repeat the quick fix but skip removing the **1,500 repeated rows**: the AUC jumps to **0.806**. It looks like an improvement of nearly 0.09, far more than any cleaning gave, and it is **fake**: the same customers sit in both the training and the test rows, so the model is graded on people it has already seen. A score that rises when you do less work should alarm you. This is why de-duplication comes first and why a number you cannot explain is not good news. The 70% of the job spent on reading and cleaning data is mostly this: protecting every later number from quietly being wrong. From here the module's lessons cover each step in depth, and the rest of the course builds the systems that depend on them.",
